{"tool_name":"as2ts","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"as2ts","home":"http://proteinmodel.org/","license":"Unlicense","summary":"This system consists of servers for protein structure analysis and modelling.","addition_date":"2017-02-10T11:34:18Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:03:22.814345Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:as2ts","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"adamz@llnl.gov","name":"Adam Zemla","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2481"},{"term":"Protein modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0477"},{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2406"},{"term":"Protein threading","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0302"},{"term":"Structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2480"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"AS2TS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkg571","metadata":{"abstract":"We present the LGA (Local-Global Alignment) method, designed to facilitate the comparison of protein structures or fragments of protein structures in sequence dependent and sequence independent modes. The LGA structure alignment program is available as an online service at http://PredictionCenter.llnl.gov/local/lga. Data generated by LGA can be successfully used in a scoring function to rank the level of similarity between two structures and to allow structure classification when many proteins are being analyzed. LGA also allows the clustering of similar fragments of protein structures.","authors":[{"name":"Zemla A."}],"citationCount":856,"date":"2003-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"LGA: A method for finding 3D similarities in protein structures"},"pmcid":"PMC168977","pmid":"12824330"},{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gki457","metadata":{"abstract":"We present a set of programs and a website designed to facilitate protein structure comparison and protein structure modeling efforts. Our protein structure analysis and comparison services use the LGA (local-global alignment) program to search for regions of local similarity and to evaluate the level of structural similarity between compared protein structures. To facilitate the homology-based protein structure modeling process, our AL2TS service translates given sequence-structure alignment data into the standard Protein Data Bank (PDB) atom records (coordinates). For a given sequence of amino acids, the AS2TS (amino acid sequence to tertiary structure) system calculates (e.g. using PSI-BLAST PDB analysis) a list of the closest proteins from the PDB, and then a set of draft 3D models is automatically created. Web services are available at http:// as2ts.llnl.gov/. \u00a9 2005 Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Barsky D."},{"name":"Kuczmarski T."},{"name":"Rama D."},{"name":"Sawicka D."},{"name":"Slezak T."},{"name":"Torres C."},{"name":"Zemla A."},{"name":"Zhou C.E."}],"citationCount":39,"date":"2005-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"AS2TS system for protein structure modeling and analysis"},"pmcid":"PMC1160218","pmid":"15980437","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein folds and structural domains","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736"},{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2814"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"},{"term":"Structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0081"},{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"AS2TS","home":"https://bio.tools/as2ts","license":"Unlicense","summary":"This system consists of servers for protein structure analysis and modelling.","tool_type":